---
description: GitNexus-backed modification admission — watcher decides
alwaysApply: true
---

- Before writing a new reusable abstraction, search GitNexus and inspect symbol context/processes.
- Prefer reuse or modification when an existing symbol fits.
- If the Modification Contract does not permit the new file, symbol, or dependency, run `orch admission request`. Do not create it until the watcher approves.
- Workers never approve their own admission requests. Strong exact hits skip the LLM.
- ORCH audits the final git + GitNexus diff independently; hiding a create does not work.
- Do not add a second code graph or homemade symbol catalog.
